    "result_text": "Full suite passes. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a read-only `displayName` field to the owner API response, formatted as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `displayName` read-only property to the `Owner` response schema (the DTO is code-generated from this spec at build time).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../util/PersonNameFormatter.java`** (new) \u2014 A small, single-responsibility formatter, following the existing `TelephoneNormalizer`/`EmailNormalizer` utility pattern, that turns first/last names into `\"LastName, FirstName\"`.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Mapped `displayName` on `toOwnerDto` via the formatter, so it's populated consistently for every response path (create, get, list).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComputesDisplayName` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
